#%Module1.0
##
## IRIS researcher tools: `module load iris` puts iris-view and iris-compare
## on the PATH, from the system clone, which researchers can read; they
## can't read the dev clone. It prepends one folder and does nothing else:
## the scripts load Python themselves. Katana's system module tree links
## to the system clone's copy of this file, so a git pull there deploys it.
## See docs/adr/0003-researcher-tools-ship-as-an-environment-module.md.
##
## Tested on Katana by module/tests/test_module.sh (see AGENTS.md).

proc ModulesHelp {} {
    puts stderr "IRIS: iris-view <run directory> views a run in napari;"
    puts stderr "iris-compare compares your runs in MLflow."
    puts stderr "Run them in a terminal in a Virtual Desktop."
}

module-whatis "IRIS: iris-view and iris-compare, to view and compare imaging runs"

prepend-path PATH /srv/scratch/katana_ai/iris/code/module/bin
